orchestration/state/auto_run.json:19:  "failure_report": "FAIL\n\nPhase 12\u2019s audit is not sufficiently fail-closed for \u201cfull validation.\u201d\n\nEvidence:\n\n- `run_audit()` computes the dataset SHA-256 but never compares it with an approved expected hash. A modified 3,800-row dataset satisfying basic schema checks would pass.\n- Prediction and metric hashes are merely recorded, not verified against preserved `artifact_hashes.json` manifests.\n- Evaluation dates are not parsed or checked for chronology, uniqueness, expected split boundaries, fold boundaries, or correspondence with source dates.\n- Saved `actual` values are not reconciled with source `Consumption` values. Mutated actuals plus correspondingly regenerated metrics could pass.\n- Phase 8\u2019s `selected_model` metric validation is explicitly skipped.\n- Tests only exercise the successful path; there are no tamper/failure tests for dataset changes, artifact changes, invalid dates, incorrect actuals, malformed folds, or hash mismatches.\n- Git inspection found only the expected Phase 12 additions and `STATUS.md` update; `git diff --check` passed.\n- Phase 0\u201311 checkpoint files parse as strict schema-v2 PASS checkpoints, and the validated commit chain is present.\n- The supplied execution environment was read-only and had no writable temporary directory, preventing an independent pytest rerun. This is not the primary reason for failure; the static audit defects above are independently sufficient.\n\nREQUIRED_CORRECTIONS:\n\n1. Compare the source dataset hash against the previously approved canonical dataset hash and fail on mismatch.\n2. Validate audited artifacts against their preserved hash manifests, not merely report newly calculated hashes.\n3. Parse every prediction date and verify uniqueness, chronology, expected evaluation boundaries, expected row counts, and chronological CV fold structure.\n4. Join predictions to the canonical dataset by date and require every saved `actual` value to match `Consumption`.\n5. Validate Phase 8 `selected_model` predictions and metrics using the preserved fold-specific winner information.\n6. Add negative tests proving the audit fails for dataset tampering, prediction/metric tampering, incorrect actual values, duplicate or reordered dates, invalid fold assignments, and manifest hash mismatches.\n7. Regenerate the Phase 12 report and rerun the focused and full test suites after these corrections.",
